{
  "table_id": "Table_S25",
  "display_number": "S25",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S25. Split-sample recalibration and held-out validation of the CHARLS-adapted PhenoAge.",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Note. Participants were assigned to training and held-out partitions in a two-thirds/one-third split. The table reports participant-wave observation counts and event-positive test observations, not unique participants or deaths. A separate score was recalibrated by elastic-net Cox regression (α as shown; 5-fold cross-validation within the training data). C-statistics are Harrell’s concordance from Cox models; ΔC is the increment over age alone; HR is the age-adjusted hazard ratio per s.d. of the recalibrated score. The full and reduced specifications contain nine and seven predictors. The reduced set removes only immune_balance and rdw_synthetic; the cystatin-C-derived albumin proxy remains. This separately recalibrated score did not reconstruct or externally validate the stored primary BAA. Abbreviations: BAA, biological age acceleration; CI, confidence interval; HR, hazard ratio."
  ],
